<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liuvigild</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 568–586</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Leovigild</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liuvigild (Leovigild) was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> from about 568 to 586 and the main architect of their kingdom in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> his capital, fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> in the south, subdued the Cantabrians and in 585 annexed the Suebic kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>. An Arian, he faced the revolt of his Catholic son Hermenegild, whom he defeated in 584.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liuvigild.jpg" alt="Liuvigild" width="320" height="152" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: You may select the license of your choice. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leovigild_CNG_97-722237.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
